{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/36196-wr20-risen-the-vampire-physical-disciplines","id":36196,"title":"Wr20, Risen & the Vampire Physical Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T23:49:27-08:00","id":36196,"title":"Wr20, Risen & the Vampire Physical Disciplines","content":"With Rich &quot;Deadguy&quot; Dansky blowing into the forums like a minor maelstrom, I thought this might be a good time to resurrect a topic from the old forums, namely the use of <i>Vampire</i>'s physical Disciplines in <i>The Risen</i>. For those of you that don't know, Fortitude, Potence, Celerity, and Obfuscate were available to the Risen as listed in their book. The problem was, there was no write-up for it. It was assumed that everyone had a copy of <i>Vampire</i> sitting around to flip through (not an unlikely assumption). Well, the idea was kicked around to do something about that, whether it be add those write-ups into the Risen book or something else. I went with the something else.<br /> <br /> The idea intrigued me. Reading through my Risen book again, I tried my hand at crafting an Arcanos specifically for the Risen to mimic <i>Vampire</i>'s Disciplines, but without needing to include their text. This is what I came up with: Formidable Corpus (or Vigor Mortis, as I like to call it. Because a good pun is a good pun), written in an approximation of the style from <i>The Risen</i>. <hr /><b>Formidable Corpus</b><br /> Coming back from beyond the Shroud is no small feat, but is only the first step in the Risen's quest. Sometimes, the body needs to be up to the task, whatever that task might be. The Risen's physical body gains several advantages from its reanimated state. The Risen's muscles are constantly constricted, giving them the appearance that they are always flexing.<br /> <u><b>Basic Abilities:</b></u><br /> <b>Statue</b>: No breath, no heartbeat, no mundane, mortal concerns of the body - the Risen can remain unobtrusive and unnoticed if they can keep their Shadow in check. System: The Risen can hide and move (very) slowly in shadows and darkness without being observed - any onlookers simply glance over them.<br /> <b>Everyman</b>: The Risen looks almost exactly like, but not quite, their former self. It is enough to convince co-workers and acquaintances that they've mistaken them for someone else, but will not work on loved ones. System: This power is always active if the Risen wishes it so.<br /> <b>\u2022 Corpse Grip</b>: Punching a hole in the lid of your coffin, crawling out from under six feet of dirt (if you're lucky), or shattering the granite in your mausoleum all requires strength. Who knows how many Risen lay in their tombs, unable to get out?<br /> System: The Risen adds 1 additional, automatic success to all Strength related rolls. Costs 1 Pathos.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Resilient Cadaver</b>: The human body is tough - a human body without all its soft, squishy inside parts is even tougher.<br /> System: The Risen adds 1 additional, automatic success to all Stamina related rolls. Costs 1 Pathos.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Death Wind</b>: For a brief moment, the Risen moves in a blur, almost too fast to see.<br /> System: The Risen may take 1 full, additional action, including movement, at no penalty. Costs 1 Pathos and 1 Willpower.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Robust Remains</b>: The strength of the reanimated dead is legendary. This power replaces Corpse Grip.<br /> System: The Risen adds 3 additional, automatic successes to all Strength related rolls. Costs 2 Pathos.<br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Stalwart Skeleton</b>: It takes a lot to put down someone tough enough to come back from death, but sometimes the unholy revenge-machine is <i>too</i> tough. This replaces Resilient Cadaver.<br /> System: The Risen adds 3 additional, automatic successes to all Stamina related rolls, and also may now soak aggravated damage. This power costs 2 Pathos and the Risen gains 1 point of Angst for each point of aggravated damage soaked in this manner (the normal &quot;doubling&quot; of Angst for Risen does not apply). <hr /><br /> The idea behind the design was that the physical Disciplines (Fortitude, Celerity, and Potence) basically just make one &quot;better&quot; at higher levels - a simple, linear progression of basically +1 at each level. Rather than having three separate tracks for physical augmentation, why not a single Arcanos that gives most players what they want anyway, and fits better with the theme? With the added bonus of curtailing any abuse of Celerity. Allowing Risen to soak Aggravated damage at the highest level also gives something for the player to strive for in addition to &quot;just more successes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obfuscate was the hardest to fit in this design, but after hashing it out for a while, I didn't see the Risen having much use for <i>Cloak the Gathering</i> or any of the higher level powers (which they shouldn't technically have access to, anyway). Rather, I thought that altering one's appearance didn't fit with the theme, nor did mimicry. What most people want is to hide in shadows and/or <i>Vanish From the Mind's Eye</i>. The latter is very powerful, and may make a suitable alternate Art.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 06-12-2014, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T12:29:42-08:00","id":36987,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I remember this from the old forums. Thanks for re-posting it here. If I'm in a spot to do something with Risen, I'm definitely using this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My personal rule; if I need more than one corebook for a session, it's time to re-think the story's direction. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:47:37-08:00","id":37029,"title":"","content":"As the one who started the thread on the old forums, I applaud this. I would note, though, that by the time the Guildbooks were done with them, the regular Arcanoi had \u201cmultiple tracks\u201d each. I\u2019d expect the \u201comnibus edition\u201d nature of Wraith20 to likewise present multiple tracks for every Arcanos, with players freely being able to mix and match as it suits their concepts. As such, I\u2019d expect a multi-track \u201cVigor Mortus\u201d Arcanos as well; and strength/stamina/speed/stealth provides a solid grounding for multiple tracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:37:54-07:00","id":446147,"title":"","content":"I like this. I like the pun for a title, however it doesn't feel congruent with the (mostly) one-word names of the other Arcanoi: Argos, Fatalism, Keening, etc. Perhaps Vitalitas or something suggesting the body would be better? Or just Vitality?<br /> <br /> The new Arcanos reminds me of Demon Shintai, which seems appropriate, given how Kuei-jin are similar to the risen. Might I suggest that the new power also channel the Shadow, thus calling on a catharsis roll? I'd bump up the extra dice benefit in exchange, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:42:25-07:00","id":446168,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, it could grant Angst? That might be a better deal, as wraiths don't spend Demon Chi or channel the P'o in the same way as the Kuei-jin. As risen must make a pact with their Shadows to rise, however, it would seem logical that the power carries some karmic cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}